WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.830
Before a football season, a team sets a target: win the league, or just avoid relegation. A business does the same. Its targets are called objectives.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:20.250
Objectives give the owner and staff a clear direction, motivate them, and give a target to check progress against.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:27.242
Financial objectives are about money: survival, profit, sales, market share, and financial security.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:40.836
Non-financial objectives are not mainly about money: social objectives, personal satisfaction, challenge, independence and control. A social objective aims to help society or the environment, such as cutting waste.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:49.557
Objectives also change as a business evolves: because of market conditions, new technology, its own results, new laws, or growth and new owners.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:59.883
Step one: decide whether the objective is financial or non-financial. Watch out: survival and market share are both financial.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:05.451
Step two: find what the owner or business in the case actually wants, using a detail from the case.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:13.847
Step three: in an explain answer, give one point, then ask so what, twice. That gives one point and two linked steps.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:27.926
Here is a real question from Paper two in November 2025, about Samsung. Explain one advantage to a business of having a social objective. It is worth three marks.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:34.386
Mark one is the advantage. A social objective can improve the business's reputation.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:45.710
Mark two explains why. When Samsung is seen to help society, customers are more likely to trust and like the brand.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:55.760
Mark three gives the consequence. More people may choose its phones and televisions instead of rivals such as Apple, so its sales rise.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:04.570
Mistake one: calling survival or market share non-financial. Both are financial objectives.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:14.925
Mistake two: defining social objective when the question asks for an advantage. A definition is not an advantage, so it earns no marks here.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:33.357
Now you try. Maya opens a small bakery. She wants to stay open through her first year, and she gives leftover bread to a local shelter every evening. Which objective is financial, and which is non-financial? Pause and decide.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:45.254
Staying open through her first year is survival, a financial objective. Giving bread to the shelter helps the community, so it is a social objective, which is non-financial.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:56.776
Remember the method: sort the objective, fit it to the business in the case, then build one point with two linked steps. Now try the practice questions for this type.
